# Elided prepositions and conjunctions (apocope before a vowel), Round 7.
# The classical stemlibs carry only the full forms; Koine texts (Apostolic
# Fathers) use elided spellings (δι', κατ', ...) that Morpheus could not
# analyze at all. Lemmas match the existing full-form entries exactly so both
# spellings share one lemma for frequency ranking. Hand-curated source file
# (picked up automatically by the nomind build: stemsrc/nom.* glob).

:le:a)po/
:wd:a)p prep
:wd:a)f prep

:le:e)pi/
:wd:e)p prep
:wd:e)f prep

:le:kata/
:wd:kat prep
:wd:kaq prep

:le:para/
:wd:par prep

:le:meta/
:wd:met prep
:wd:meq prep

:le:u(po/
:wd:u(p prep
:wd:u(f prep

:le:dia/
:wd:di prep

# Papyrological elision (Round 8): ἐγ for ἐκ before a vowel, x16 in the
# PapyGreek treebanks.
:le:e)k
:wd:e)g prep

:le:a)lla/
:wd:a)ll conj
